---
// /en/sos/ (правка 2026-07-13, «Правки-5» п.8): аудитория - Европа (DE главный
// ориентир, NL, ES); США/Канада убраны. Каталоги findahelpline/befrienders
// оставлены для остальных стран EU. noindex, ссылка SOS - в футере EN-страниц.
import Page from '../../../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
  title="SOS: where to get help right now · Valeriy Karasaev"
  description="If things are very hard right now: emergency numbers and crisis lines in Germany, the Netherlands and Spain, support groups, confidential psychiatric help."
  lang="en"
  noindex={true}
  hideCta={true}
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <div class="kicker">SOS</div>
    <h1 class="page-title">If things are very hard right now</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      There are states you should not stay alone with: when it hits so hard you can't breathe,
      when violence has happened, when you can't stop drinking, or when you fear for your own life.
      Help exists, it is close, and much of it is free and anonymous. This page collects
      places you can turn to right now, wherever in Europe you live.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">01</span><span class="meta-label">By phone</span></div>
  <div class="spec">
    <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Immediate danger to life (EU)</span><span class="spec-val">112 · 24/7, free, any EU country</span></div>
    <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Germany · TelefonSeelsorge</span><span class="spec-val">0800 111 0 111 or 0800 111 0 222 · 24/7, free</span></div>
    <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Netherlands · 113 Zelfmoordpreventie</span><span class="spec-val">113 or 0800-0113 · 24/7, free</span></div>
    <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Spain · Línea 024</span><span class="spec-val">024 · 24/7, free</span></div>
    <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Other EU countries · directory</span><span class="spec-val"><a href="https://findahelpline.com" rel="noopener" style="color: var(--gold); text-decoration: none;">findahelpline.com</a></span></div>
    <div class="spec-row"><span class="spec-key">Emotional support worldwide</span><span class="spec-val"><a href="https://befrienders.org" rel="noopener" style="color: var(--gold); text-decoration: none;">befrienders.org</a></span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      You don't need a «serious enough» reason to call. Feeling bad is already a reason.
      They will listen, help you get through the acute moment and tell you where to go next.
      In Germany, TelefonSeelsorge also offers <a href="https://online.telefonseelsorge.de" rel="noopener">chat and email counselling</a>;
      the directories above cover the rest of Europe, in local languages and English.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">02</span><span class="meta-label">If violence has happened</span></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Domestic, physical, sexualized - any kind. It is not something to «endure»,
      and it is not your fault. In Germany, the Hilfetelefon «Gewalt gegen Frauen»
      (116 016, 24/7, free) counsels in 18 languages including English and Russian,
      and will point you to the nearest crisis center. Similar lines exist across the EU -
      search «domestic violence helpline» plus your country. These services help legally,
      psychologically and sometimes with temporary shelter, free and confidentially.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">03</span><span class="meta-label">If the problem is alcohol or substances</span></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      There are communities that have been helping people climb out for decades: Alcoholics
      Anonymous, Narcotics Anonymous, and for those who grew up next to addiction - ACA
      (Adult Children of Alcoholics). It really works. Meetings are free and anonymous,
      in person and online, in many languages. Search «AA / NA / ACA» plus your city -
      meeting schedules are open. You can come just to listen: nobody will make you speak.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">04</span><span class="meta-label">If you need medical help</span></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Severe depression, panic attacks, intrusive thoughts of death, states where reality
      «floats» - these are treatable, and the one who treats them is a psychiatrist.
      Seeing a psychiatrist is ordinary care for your health, like seeing a cardiologist.
    </p>
    <p>
      If confidentiality worries you: private clinics and psychiatrists in private practice
      see patients confidentially. It costs money, but it removes the main fear that keeps
      people from reaching help.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="meta-line"><span class="meta-num">05</span><span class="meta-label">How I can help</span></div>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Honestly: I am a psychologist, not a doctor. I don't prescribe medication, don't work
      with severe psychiatric conditions and don't work with children. But over the years
      of practice I have built a wide network of colleagues - psychiatrists and psychotherapists
      I trust.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you don't know where to go with your situation - <a href="https://t.me/vkarasaev">write to me</a>.
      I will help you get oriented and recommend a specialist. It is free and comes
      with no obligations.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
